Decisions: BS-40293 rejected: Irish glune fri talmain is military posture, Sanskrit janubhyam bhu tale sthitah is reverence; ordinary knees/ground relation, and Irish doesetar is not a secure cognate of Sanskrit stha despite automatic mapping. BS-a32fb rejected: nuts/sloes/apples versus berries/nuts/sour apples, ordinary gathering list; same Irish text repeats fruits but no distinctive shared formula established. BS-bf5c6 rejected: cu dian is an epithet in the hero name context, Greek kyon dietai is a hunting simile with finite chase verb; plausible cognates but insufficient evidence against generic hound swiftness/pursuit. BS-c191a rejected: parent/cattle vocabulary does not establish congruent phrase or speech act; difficult Irish wording not silently emended. BS-ea337 rejected: blegon bo and mjolka kyr are ordinary milking descriptions, with no shared distinctive figure. Other bundles show isolated cognates, erroneous mappings, incongruent contexts, or same-branch parallels only.
